    "note": "HPE's own row, not the model name. The 1950 QuickSpecs (v10, 2018) JG962A Technical Specifications table prints \"PoE power 370 W PoE+\", maximum power rating 425 W, and \"When supplemented with the use of an HPE RPS1600 Redundant Power System, up to 720W of PoE+ can be supplied\" - so 370 W is the internal-supply allocation and the 720 W needs the separately sold JG136A RPS. I/O row: \"24 RJ-45 auto-negotiating 10/100/1000 PoE+ ports\", \"2 SFP+ fixed 1000/10000 SFP+ ports\", \"2 RJ-45 1/10GBASE-T ports\", plus \"Additional ports and slots: 1 RJ-45 console port to access limited CLI port\" - that console is the reason the box declares `cli`, and it was missing from the model. 370 W across 24 PoE+ ports is 15.4 W average."
  },
